  "seoTitle": "Prabowo Subianto National Teacher Day 2026 Announcements",
  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto addresses teacher welfare during National Teacher Day, noting plans for wage increases, international training, and facilities.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto indicated plans to increase teacher salaries while acknowledging that the exact timeline remains under consideration.",
    "The government plans to enhance educational access through new remote learning studios and sending over 3,000 teachers abroad for training by 2027.",
    "Parliamentary members have proposed increasing teacher salaries to Rp20 million monthly and advocated for updated regulations for older teacher applicants."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "During the commemoration of National Teacher Day 2026, President Prabowo Subianto held discussions regarding the professional welfare and development of educators in Indonesia. While expressing a commitment to raising teacher salaries, the President noted that a specific implementation schedule has not yet been confirmed. The government is also preparing initiatives to expand long-distance education access through the development of dedicated teacher studios and plans to send 3,350 teachers to nine different countries for professional training in 2027. Additionally, the administration is considering the potential reclamation of millions of hectares of illegally controlled land as a possible funding source for public welfare, including potential teacher compensation. Parliamentary representatives continue to monitor these developments, emphasizing the need for regulatory updates for teachers over 35 years old and proposing new fiscal schemes to support teacher income.",
